nt":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/4961","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/4961","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/4961.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/4961.patch","merged_at":"2018-04-25T16:27:45Z"},"body":"Fixes #4960 \r\nFixes #4853 \r\n\r\nThe first issue is fixed by:\r\n* Defining a _new_ `Var` if there is a `self` assignment with an explicit type in a subclass.\r\n* Applying `check_compatibility_super` to `RefExpr` lvalues, not only `NameExpr`.\r\n\r\nThe second issue is fixed by adding two dependencies:\r\n* If a variable is defined in class, recheck the current target (without recursing to methods).\r\n* If a variable is defined via `self` in a method, recheck the defining method only.\r\n* The above two are only added for classes with user-defined bases (this allows to avoid trivial deps that would only \"pollute\" many tests, but are useless in practice).\r\n\r\nThere was one more thing I tried to fix, there seems to be an inconsistency that lvalues corresponding to `self` definitions have their kind set to `None` instead of `MDEF` (like for names defined in class). But I abandoned this because some code relies on this. I think we can clean this in an upcoming refactoring.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/4961/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"htt